course: dictionary
lesson: 4181
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Goldfish» is one of them. It can mean a small orange or gold-coloured fish kept as a pet, or it can describe a place where everyone can see what you are doing.
explain: Read the words around it. «It reminds her of the goldfish bowl she upset last week, and she quickly scoops them back in» is about a real bowl, because you can upset a bowl and scoop things back in. The clues are in the other words, not in the word goldfish itself.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If "a small orange fish" still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. If it does not, look for the second meaning, and check a dictionary when you are not sure.
fact: Goldfish means a small orange or gold-coloured fish, often kept as a pet in a tank or pond.
fact: «A goldfish bowl» can also mean a place where everyone can see what you are doing.
fact: Goldfish need a large tank with clean water and a filter, not a small round bowl.
fact: Goldfish can live for over ten years if they are well looked after.
fact: Myth: goldfish do not have a three-second memory; they can learn and remember for months.
exercise: «Goldfish need a large tank with clean water and a filter.» What does goldfish mean in this sentence? | A gold coin given as a prize | A place where everyone can see you | A green weed that grows in ponds | *A small orange fish kept as a pet
exercise: Mia says, «Our class is a goldfish bowl this week.» What does she mean? | The classroom is wet and cold | *Everyone can see what everyone is doing | Everyone is hungry | The class has a new pet fish
exercise: Which sentence uses goldfish to mean a real fish? | Her job is a goldfish bowl, where the boss watches every move. | Everyone in the office is in a goldfish bowl this week. | *Goldfish can live for over ten years if they are well looked after.
test: Goldfish need a large tank with clean water and a filter. What is a good home for a goldfish? | A plastic bag from the fair | *A large tank with clean water and a filter | A small round bowl | A dry box on a shelf
test: Someone says, «A goldfish has a three-second memory.» Is this true? | Yes, in three seconds it forgets everything | Yes, it only remembers when it is hungry | *No, goldfish can learn and remember for months | No, goldfish cannot learn anything at all
exam: In «Everyone watched her, like a goldfish in a bowl», what does goldfish bowl mean? | A pond full of weeds | A gold prize at the fair | A small round bowl with a fish in it | *A place where everyone can see what you are doing
